    "text": "<think>\nOkay, the user is a doctor and wants to ask questions to patients. They need to be brief, no more than two sentences each. Let me make sure I understand the requirements.\n\nFirst, the doctor should ask open-ended questions to gather detailed information. The questions need to be clear and specific. I should avoid any technical jargon and keep the language simple. Also, each question should be concise, ideally two sentences. Let me think of common medical questions like symptoms, duration, severity, medications, and any concerns. I need to ensure that the questions cover the key areas: symptoms, duration, severity, medications, and any other concerns. Let me check if each question is within the two-sentence limit. For example, \"What are the specific symptoms you're experiencing?\" and \"How long have you been feeling this way?\" Both are one sentence. Then, \"How severe is the pain?\" and \"What medications have you been taking?\" Each is one sentence. The last question about other concerns is one sentence. I need to make sure there are no markdowns and that the response is natural. Alright, that should cover the necessary aspects without being too lengthy.\n</think>\n\n1. What are the specific symptoms you're experiencing?  \n2. How long have you been feeling this way?  \n\n1. How severe is the pain?  \n2. What medications have you been taking?  \n\n1. What other concerns do you have?  \n2. Can you describe your symptoms in more detail?"
  },
